new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e7c84ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/AUTH-SETUP.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Reboot 27.11 authentication DLL - candidate 1
+
+This is a compiled Tellurium derivative for a backend running on the same PC
+at `http://127.0.0.1:3551`. It is experimental: compilation and synthetic tests
+do not establish compatibility with the Fortnite 27.11 executable or EOS SDK.
+
+## Install
+
+1. Close both Fortnite instances before changing DLL selections.
+2. Extract the downloaded artifact ZIP into a permanent folder, for example
+   `C:\Reboot2711\Auth`.
+3. Open Reboot Launcher -> Settings -> Internal files.
+4. Beside **Authentication patcher**, click the folder button and select
+   **Reboot-27.11-Auth.dll**. This replaces the selected Cobalt/Sinum auth DLL.
+5. Start the existing local backend on port 3551, then launch Fortnite 27.11.
+
+| Launcher field | DLL |
+| --- | --- |
+| Authentication patcher | Reboot-27.11-Auth.dll from this package |
+| Unreal engine patcher | Existing Reboot-27.11-Client.dll |
+| Game server type | Custom |
+| Game server | Existing Reboot-27.11-Server.dll |
+
+No copy into Fortnite's installation directory is necessary: select the extracted
+DLL with the launcher's folder button. This package contains only the auth DLL;
+the client and server DLLs are separate artifacts.
+
+## Diagnostics
+
+Press Win+R and open `%TEMP%\Reboot-27.11-Auth-startup.log` after a launch.
+The file is replaced on each new initialization. Start one game instance at a
+time while diagnosing a failure. The log records stages and relative addresses,
+without request URLs, passwords, session tokens, or command-line arguments.
+
+- Allocator missing: the executable's allocator signature needs investigation.
+- Stage 1: loaded PE sections could not be read.
+- Stage 2: the request-function string reference was not found.
+- Stage 3: the request function could not be identified.
+- Stage 4: a pointer to that function was not found in the request table.
+- READY: both hooks were installed, but login is not yet verified.
+- First URL redirected: that request was rewritten; backend response and login
+  still need to succeed.
+
+Each discovery stage has a 30-second retry budget with pauses. A failure displays
+a message instead of proceeding through a missing pointer. The main and EOS
+request locations are both discovered before either hook is installed.
+
+The earlier **Object class was not found in GObjects** error comes from the
+separate Erbium client/server initialization. This auth build does not resolve
+that SDK lookup. If that error returns after authentication succeeds, collect
+`%TEMP%\Reboot-27.11-Client-startup.log` or the corresponding Server log.
+
+`5.4.0-29739262+++Fortnite+Release-27.11` contains the engine version (5.4.0),
+changelist (29739262), and game release (27.11); those are different fields.
+
+## Build and provenance
+
+Based on Ploosh's Tellurium, commit
+`8750678312c011888b82878fb1d011b97b33fff5`:
+https://github.com/plooshi/Tellurium/tree/8750678312c011888b82878fb1d011b97b33fff5
+
+Upstream is BSD 3-Clause; the original LICENSE is included in the binary and
+source packages. Changes add bounded scanners and startup waits, Windows unwind
+function lookup with the upstream prologue fallback, checked request-table writes,
+startup diagnostics, and bounded URL handling. The Release x64 build uses the
+static C++ runtime. Optional memory and push-widget patches are disabled.
+
+This candidate retains upstream's request-object ABI assumptions, including the
+EOS SetURL virtual index 10 and the game SetURL fallback index 10. Runtime logs
+report the chosen index. These are not validated against the user's executable.
+No claim of full Fortnite 27.11 support or a working multiplayer match is made.
+
+The matching source artifact includes this document and tests. On Windows with
+Visual Studio 2022 C++ tools installed, run from a Developer Command Prompt:
+
+```
+msbuild Tellurium.sln /m /t:Rebuild /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=x64 /p:TargetName=Reboot-27.11-Auth
+```
+
+The reproducible GitHub workflow in EmilyUwU666/reboot-2711 pins the upstream
+commit, applies `build-support/auth-candidate1.patch`, runs scanner and Windows
+hook/URL tests, builds the DLL, validates its x64 PE headers, and records SHA256.
+`BUILD-INFO.txt` in the binary artifact identifies the exact workflow commit.
